steps":{"digest":"4ad588e382b5e66a69528df114ce6f6e7bf5a862cd319d4ebfa579d7486450d1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--plan/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":7716},"state":{"digest":"38f018ee9cdd65b2c9e1ab434c18a9bebff0ed23fb853a10672cda14b09c1680","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":210}},"finished_at":"2026-11-12T22:02:09.321845+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--plan","local_name":"sase-1sl.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1sl","agent_clan_generation":"20261112164912","agent_session":"sase-1sl.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"sase-1sl.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1sl[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Bound the runner-slot capacity scan and make the TUI GC policy [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]cost-adaptive[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The sase TUI and waiting agent runners stop burning CPU and memory [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]on full-archive capacity scans: a warm capacity scan costs [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]milliseconds instead of 23 s, the TUI holds under 15% of one core [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and a bounded heap on athena, and full GC collections respect a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]duty-cycle bound.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]capacity_scan_tui_runaway.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/capacity_scan_tui_runaway.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1sl[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1sl/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core: capacity-only scan cost scales with live records, [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]not archive size[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-capacity-scan[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-capacity-scan: in the linked sase-core repo, add a statx-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live-marker precheck plus meta-light closure classification (and, per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the verdict_cache decision, a sticky never-live verdict cache) to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity_only scanner path, with parity tests and a scan-cost bench [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]guarding identical retained records.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ratchet the core pin and re-measure the scan on the real [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]archive[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sase-adopt-pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-capacity-scan[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-adopt-pin: move sase-core-revision.txt past the core commit, adopt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]any new scan option in runner_slots/_scan.py, and re-measure cold/warm [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity scans and runner-cache behavior on athena against the 22.9 s [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI GC policy: full collections respect a duty-cycle bound[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-duty-cycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-duty-cycle: record each full collection's duration in gc_policy.py [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and defer the next full collection by last-pause times a duty factor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](clamped), applying the floor to idle and backstop triggers alike, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fake-clock unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Measured verification on athena and residual-leak attribution[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]athena-soak[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-adopt-pin, gc-duty-cycle[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]athena-soak: soak a TUI instance on athena for at least an hour under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real agent load, verify CPU, rchar, RSS, GC-pause, and runner-CPU [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]targets against the 2026-11-12 baseline, and attribute any residual RSS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]growth with the GC census.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1sl","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1sl.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-1sl.1"},"source_run_id":"run-8886a946aa5c5c16d93dc2fecf9d527a","started_at":"2026-11-12T21:51:31.053202+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":["prompt"],"restartable":false},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"ca769eb90e784fb1979675654cb57b9959ce24e0aacfa643b512b4d0015dd747","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--mon/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"b2b106cfb46fe9efd7f3f288780e3b2290ba2072afbdd8d1d8aa782c1b478b44","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--mon/meta.json","size_bytes":723},"state":{"digest":"ecb9117a44e967ce4da29f3ee3376516eb5ab47914e7ec400751844013cff2c3","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--mon/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1sl.1--mon","local_name":"sase-1sl.1--mon","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1sl","agent_clan_generation":"20261112164912","agent_session":"sase-1sl.1","agent_session_role":"mon","bead_id":"sase-1sl.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","